  <h1>Know Your DIGIPIN — India Post's Digital Address Code</h1>
  <p class="updated">Updated 28 September 2026 · Free tool · No login required</p>

  <div class="answer">
    <strong>DIGIPIN (Digital Postal Index Number)</strong> is the Government of India's official digital address
    system. It gives every <strong>roughly 4m × 4m spot in India</strong> — including places with no formal address —
    a unique <strong>10-character code</strong> calculated from the location's latitude and longitude. A full DIGIPIN
    looks like <strong>39J-438-TJC7</strong> and pinpoints a location to about 3.8 metres, anywhere in India.
  </div>

