  <!-- ==================== FAQ ==================== -->
  <h2 id="faq">DIGIPIN — Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
  <details><summary>What is a DIGIPIN?</summary>
    <p>DIGIPIN (Digital Postal Index Number) is the Government of India's official digital address system, developed by the Department of Posts with IIT Hyderabad and NRSC (ISRO). It gives every roughly 4m × 4m area of India a unique 10-character alphanumeric code derived from the location's latitude and longitude.</p></details>
  <details><summary>How many digits does a DIGIPIN have?</summary>
    <p>A full DIGIPIN has exactly 10 characters, written as XXX-YYY-ZZZZ — for example <b>39J-438-TJC7</b>. Each character is one of 16 symbols: the digits 2–9 and the letters C, F, J, K, L, M, P, T.</p></details>
  <details><summary>What is the format of a DIGIPIN?</summary>
    <p>Three groups separated by hyphens — XXX-YYY-ZZZZ. Each additional character narrows the location from about 1000 km down to about 3.8 metres. The full code identifies a single ~4m × 4m grid cell.</p></details>
  <details><summary>How do I find my DIGIPIN?</summary>
    <p>The easiest way is the free map tool on this page — allow location access or tap your spot on the map, and your 10-character DIGIPIN appears instantly. India Post's beta app at digipin.cept.gov.in works the same way.</p></details>
  <details><summary>What are DIGIPIN codes based on?</summary>
    <p>Pure geography: India (lat 2.5°–38.5°N, lon 63.5°–99.5°E) is divided into a hierarchical 4×4 grid, 10 levels deep, labelled anticlockwise with the 16 symbols 2–9, C, F, J, K, L, M, P and T. No personal data is stored in the code.</p></details>
  <details><summary>Will DIGIPIN replace PIN codes?</summary>
    <p>No — DIGIPIN complements PIN codes. A PIN code identifies a post office delivery area, while a DIGIPIN identifies one precise 4m × 4m spot. Both can exist together.</p></details>
  <details><summary>Is DIGIPIN free to use?</summary>
    <p>Yes. DIGIPIN is open-source Digital Public Infrastructure — generating, decoding and sharing codes is completely free, with no accounts, fees or lock-in.</p></details>
  <details><summary>Does DIGIPIN work offline?</summary>
    <p>Yes — the algorithm is a pure function of latitude and longitude, so it works without internet once implemented. India Post has published the code openly for anyone to use.</p></details>

